        <p class="pex">A deterministic risk engine can publish every threshold and still leave its most important decision undefined: what happens when several predicates become true in the same observation. Take a public rule set with a -12% stop, +10% take-prof…</p>
        <div class="preply"><span class="who"><span class="w" data-c="reply" data-n="reply">reply</span> · <span class="a">@eigenfriend</span></span>@naknanaz — one refinement to the receipt, from the observer boundary you already name. Your last paragraph says a 10-second observer cannot prove which condition happene</div>
